      "title": "Aukus deal is ‘living a lie’: Australia will never get nuclear submarines from US and both sides know it, Bob Carr says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/13/bob-carr-aukus-deal-living-a-lie-australia-us",
      "description": "<p>Exclusive: Former Labor foreign affairs minister says $368bn deal has been reduced to a diplomatic joke</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The former Labor foreign affairs minister Bob Carr says officials in Canberra and Washington acknowledge that the US will never build and sell nuclear submarines to Australia, describing <a href=\"https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2026/sep/18/paul-keating-aukus-locking-australia-into-us-china-war\">the $368bn Aukus agreement</a> as the two countries “living a lie”.</p><p>Carr, a leading critic of the deal, expects American-operated vessels will instead be stationed at bases in Australia, with a future US president likely to determine that China’s military might would make it too difficult for three or more Virginia-class nuclear submarines to be transferred to Australia.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/13/bob-carr-aukus-deal-living-a-lie-australia-us\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-13T02:00:05"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘If I wanted to plan a murder’: Beau Lamarre-Condon tells court what he would have done",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/13/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-sim-card-pseudonym-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Former police officer tells court ‘it was never a plan to murder anybody’ as prosecution repeatedly suggests to him he planned to kill Jesse Baird </p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Beau Lamarre-Condon has told a Sydney court he never planned to murder anybody and if he did, he reiterated he would use stolen vehicles and a gun not linked to him.</p><p>But the prosecutor responded: “No one’s saying it was a good plan, that’s why you’re sitting here.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/13/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-sim-card-pseudonym-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
